{
  title: "241 window-all is linear and lazy; window survives a step past the end"
  doc: "eu-oaz72.56: window-all (and partition-all) called count on the
        remaining list at every step, so it was O(n^2) and never terminated
        on an infinite list. window dropped `step` items with the prelude
        drop, which fails on a list shorter than `step`. Both now skip with
        a nil-safe local helper."
}

` "the target computes the right values"
passes(context): (context.result values all-true?) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :semantics
    verify: [:passes] }
semantics: {
  pa-short-tail: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] partition-all(2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5]]
  pa-exact: ([1, 2, 3, 4] partition-all(2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
  pa-empty: ([] partition-all(2)) = []
  wa-sliding: ([1, 2, 3, 4] window-all(3, 1)) = [[1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4], [3, 4], [4]]
  wa-step-gap: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window-all(2, 3)) = [[1, 2], [4, 5]]
  wa-step-past-end: ([1, 2, 3] window-all(2, 5)) = [[1, 2]]
  w-step-past-end: ([1, 2, 3] window(2, 5)) = [[1, 2]]
  w-step-gap: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] window(2, 3)) = [[1, 2], [4, 5]]
  w-exact: ([1, 2, 3, 4, 5] window(2, 2)) = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
}

` "A long finite list standing in for an infinite one, so a regression FAILs on the tick budget instead of hanging."
long: range(0, 1000000)

` "taking a few windows does not walk the list"
few-ticks(context): (context.stats.ticks < 100000) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :lazy
    verify: [:passes, :few-ticks]
    doc: "The old `window-all` counted the whole remaining list before
          yielding each window, so on an infinite list it never returned.
          Taking a few windows must cost nothing like the length of the list." }
lazy: {
  wa: (long window-all(2, 1) take(3)) = [[0, 1], [1, 2], [2, 3]]
  pa: (long partition-all(3) take(2)) = [[0, 1, 2], [3, 4, 5]]
  w: (long window(2, 3) take(2)) = [[0, 1], [3, 4]]
}

` "List length for the cost target: the linear version is far inside the budget, the quadratic one far outside it."
n: 4000

` "the cost is linear in the length of the list"
linear-cost(context): (context.stats.ticks < 1000 * n) then(:PASS, :FAIL)

` { target: :cost
    verify: [:passes, :linear-cost]
    doc: "One `count` per window over the remaining list made `window-all`
          quadratic; the tick budget is per element." }
cost: {
  pa: (range(0, n) partition-all(2) count) = n / 2
  wa: (range(0, n) window-all(2, 1) count) = n
}
